itono transaction are all again noteworthy transactions.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/02/01/stifel-financial-corp-sf-q4-2018-earnings-conferen.aspx"},{"c":"SF 2019 Q1","e":"sf","d":"2019-04-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Ronald J. Kruszewski","x":"Our advisory business generated fees of $105 million as the diversity of our business was underscored by a very strong quarter from our restructuring practice.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/04/30/stifel-financial-corp-sf-q1-2019-earnings-call-tra.aspx"},{"c":"SF 2019 Q4","e":"sf","d":"2020-01-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Ronald J. Kruszewski","x":"Some notable transactions include, in the technology space, we advised on the sale of Electro Scientific Industries to MKS and in restructuring, we advised the COFINA Puerto Rican Senior Bondholders Coalition.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/01/30/stifel-financial-corp-sf-q4-2019-earnings-call-tra.aspx"},{"c":"SF 2019 Q4","e":"sf","d":"2020-01-30","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Ronald J. Kruszewski","x":"In terms of net interest margin, we're maintaining our guidance from last quarter of 310 basis points to 320 basis points.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/01/30/stifel-financial-corp-sf-q4-2019-earnings-call-tra.aspx"},{"c":"SF 2020 Q1","e":"sf","d":"2020-04-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Ronald J. Kruszewski","x":"Revenue declined 28% due to the slowdown of activity levels in March and the fact that the first quarter of 2019 had a significant restructuring fee from miller Buckfire as work on the COFINA transaction.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/04/30/stifel-financial-corp-sf-q1-2020-earnings-call-tra.aspx"},{"c":"SF 2020 Q1","e":"sf","d":"2020-04-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Ronald J. Kruszewski","x":"Specifically, we're seeing significant increased client engagement with our restructuring team at Miller Buckfire.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/04/30/stifel-financial-corp-sf-q1-2020-earnings-call-tra.aspx"},{"c":"SF 2020 Q1","e":"sf","d":"2020-04-30","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Ronald J. Kruszewski","x":"First of all, first of all, I want to be clear when I talked about guidance, we've withdrawn our guidance as let's say as go through these comments going forward other than what Jim had said about net interest income.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/04/30/stifel-financial-corp-sf-q1-2020-earnings-call-tra.aspx"},{"c":"SF 2020 Q3","e":"sf","d":"2020-10-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Ronald J. Kruszewski","x":"In terms of verticals, the performance of our advisory business was driven by technology, industrials and restructuring.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/28/stifel-financial-corp-sf-q3-2020-earnings-call-tra/"},{"c":"SF 2020 Q3","e":"sf","d":"2020-10-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Ronald J. Kruszewski","x":"And so I think the bigger issue that's going to impact financial institutions in the next year is going to be actually the amount of business that we have to do, restructuring, doing M&A and potentially doing an infrastructure bill because of what I think is going to be a lot of stimulus.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/28/stifel-financial-corp-sf-q3-2020-earnings-call-tra/"},{"c":"SF 2021 Q2","e":"sf","d":"2021-07-28","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Ron Kruszewski","x":"As we head into the back half of this year, we are well-positioned to continue our strong performance, which is illustrated by our increased full year guidance, which I'll discuss in greater detail in a few minutes.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/28/stifel-financial-corp-sf-q2-2021-earnings-call-tra/"},{"c":"SF 2021 Q2","e":"sf","d":"2021-07-28","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Ron Kruszewski","x":"But given the strength of our results in the first half of the year, the current strength of our pipelines and my visibility into the beginning of this quarter, we believe that it is appropriate to increase our full year guidance at this time.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/28/stifel-financial-corp-sf-q2-2021-earnings-call-tra/"},{"c":"SF 2021 Q3","e":"sf","d":"2021-10-27","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Ronald J. Kruszewski","x":"And so when you model that out over two or three years, you can see just from that one line item, net interest income, how that can rightsize our capital levels, I agree we've built some capital here, but drive earnings as well.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/27/stifel-financial-corp-sf-q3-2021-earnings-call-tra/"},{"c":"SF 2025 Q4","e":"sf","d":"2026-01-28","l":"ai_spend","r":"management","s":"Ronald James Kruszewski","x":"Technology and industrial technology remain active, driven by AI and infrastructure investment, with large transactions in energy, infrastructure services, and defense being well received by the market.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/01/28/stifel-sf-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"SF 2025 Q4","e":"sf","d":"2026-01-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Ronald James Kruszewski","x":"We're doing a couple things with the sale of SIA and the European restructuring, which alone left in a vacuum drive comp ratio lower.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/01/28/stifel-sf-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"SF 2025 Q4","e":"sf","d":"2026-01-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"James Marischen","x":"We do see some potential cost savings related to that, but that's probably more of a 2027 event.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/01/28/stifel-sf-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"SF 2026 Q3","e":"sf","d":"2026-10-21","l":"cost_cuts","r":